From: OpenMandriva os-image-builder <bero@lindev.ch>
Subject: [PATCH] scripts: sign-file: include time.h for OpenSSL 4

OpenSSL 4.0 headers use time_t in public APIs without including <time.h>.
Host-tool builds of sign-file then fail with gcc 16 / -std=gnu11.

---
 scripts/sign-file.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/scripts/sign-file.c b/scripts/sign-file.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/scripts/sign-file.c
+++ b/scripts/sign-file.c
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include <getopt.h>
 #include <err.h>
 #include <arpa/inet.h>
+#include <time.h>
 #include <openssl/opensslv.h>
 #include <openssl/bio.h>
 #include <openssl/evp.h>
 #include <openssl/pem.h>
 #include <openssl/err.h>
